/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

HandleDlcConfigure: PROCEDURE (pConfigureDlCB, pError);
 DCL pConfigureDlCB SELECTOR;
 DCL ConfigureDlCB BASED pConfigureDlCB
      STRUCTURE (DlCBgenDescriptor, DlCBConfigureParams);
 DCL pdlConfDlCB BASED pConfigureDlCB
      STRUCTURE (DlCBgenDescriptor, DlCBPdlConfParams);
 DCL pError POINTER;

$IF document
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Purpose: This procedure will initialize the data link layer, 
      including: check to see if link is already active, 
      create new data link process, pass initialization 
      parameters to the data link process. Once the data
      link process has been created, all subsequent message
      will go directly to/come from that process.

 Inputs:  selector of init data link control block msg. This message
          will include the following parameters:
       link Number - local identifier specifying hardware I/O
          port.
       link speed - specifies the data rate for the physical 
          link.
       station count - specifies maximum number of stations to
          be supported on this wire.
       protocol Type - specifies type of data link protocol to
          to be loaded. 
          Currently, only SDLC Primary is available.

 Outputs: error - specifies completion status, one of: 
        Ok, out of memory, 
        dlcInvalidLinkNumber, dlcAlreadyActive.

 Algorithm: o  Check to see if valid link number value.
      o  Check to see if data link already exists.
      o  Create data link, including necessary machine variables
       and the I/O semaphore used to signal inputs to MAC
       I/O completion process (done only if one MAC per link).
      o  enable the Media access control for the link.
      o  Pass the initialization message to the new data link
       process. 
      o  Wait for reply from dlc son.
      o  Return reply to user, with appropriate error code.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
$ENDIF
 DCL error BASED pError WORD;
 DCL linkNumber BYTE;
 DCL (note, error2) WORD;
 DCL x BYTE;
 DCL (tempPID, tempMsgFormat) WORD;
 DCL tempFreeDisp BYTE;
 DCL pRecvDlCB POINTER;
 DCL recvDlCB BASED pRecvDlCB STRUCTURE (DlCBgenDescriptor,
                 DlCBioDataParams);
 DCL commExecPid WORD;
 DCL pInitDlCB SELECTOR;
 DCL initDlCB BASED pInitDlCB STRUCTURE (DlCBgenDescriptor,
                DlCBinitParams);
 DCL ConfigOption WORD;
 DCL phonelinkType BYTE;
 DO;
  error = 0;
  /* configOption control whether configure is reported to commexec */
  configOption = configureDlCB.reqError;

 /* check link number validity */
  linkNumber = ConfigureDlCB.linkNumber;
  IF (linkNumber >= maxNumberOfLinks) THEN 
    error = eDlcInvalidLinkNumber;
  ELSE IF dlcProcessId(linkNumber) <> null THEN 
    error = eDlcAlreadyExists;
  
  IF error <> 0 THEN RETURN;
 /* check protocol type validity and create dlc process */
$IF primary
  ELSE IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcPrimaryProtocol THEN
   DO;
    dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = 
      OsForkProcess(@PrimaryDlcProcess, dlcPriority,
            FALSE, dlcStackSize, @error);
   END;
$ENDIF
$IF secondary
  ELSE IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcSecondaryProtocol THEN
   DO;
    dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = 
      OsForkProcess(@SecondaryDlcProcess, dlcPriority,
            FALSE, dlcStackSize, @error);
   END;
$ENDIF
$IF phoneLink
  ELSE IF (ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcPhoneLinkProtocol) OR
  					(ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcOriginateProtocol) OR
					(ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcAnswerProtocol) OR
					(ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcOrigAndAnsProtocol) THEN
   DO; /* one process fits all */
    IF NOT phoneLinkStarted THEN
     DO;
      phoneLinkProcess = 
        OsForkProcess(@CcPdlProcess, dlcPriority,
						FALSE, pdlStackSize, @error);
      phoneLinkStarted = TRUE;
     END;
    dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = phoneLinkProcess;
   END;
$ENDIF
  ELSE error = eDlcInvalidProtocolType;

  IF error = ok THEN 
   DO;
    CALL MacEnable(linkNumber, ConfigureDlCB.linkSpeed, 
         ConfigureDlCB.ioType, ConfigureDlCB.duplexType,
         @error);
$IF phonelink
	phonelinkType = nullByte;
	IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcPhoneLinkProtocol THEN
		phonelinkType = originateAndAnswer;
	ELSE
		IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcOriginateProtocol THEN
			phonelinkType = originateOnly;
	ELSE
		IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcAnswerProtocol THEN
			phonelinkType = answerOnly;
	ELSE
		IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType = dlcOrigAndAnsProtocol THEN
			phonelinkType = originateAndAnswer;

	IF phonelinkType <> nullByte THEN
	DO;
		IF ConfigureDlCB.protocolType <> dlcPhoneLinkProtocol THEN
			CALL MacSetLineParms(linkNumber, phonelinkType,
					pdlConfDlCB.modemType, pdlConfDlCB.dialingMode, 1, 30);
		ELSE
			CALL MacSetLineParms(linkNumber, originateAndAnswer, noModem,
													touchToneType, 1, 30);
	END;
$ENDIF
   END;
  IF error = ok THEN 
   DO;
    CALL TmrConfigureTimer(pConfigureDlCB, @error);
   END;

  IF error = ok THEN 
   DO;
    tempPID = ConfigureDlCB.sourcePID;
    tempMsgFormat = ConfigureDlCB.msgFormat;
    tempFreeDisp = ConfigureDlCB.freeDisp;
    ConfigureDlCB.freeDisp = returnMsg;
    CALL GenGiveToDlc(linkNumber, (dlcConfigure OR msgRequest),
          pConfigureDlCB, @error);

/* wait for dlc Configure response */
    pConfigureDlCB = 
        SELECTOR$OF(OsReceive(dlcProcessId(linkNumber),
            (dlcConfigure OR msgResponse),
            10000, @note, @error));
    IF error = ok THEN
     DO;
      IF ConfigureDlCB.reqError = ok THEN
       DO;
$IF debugging
        IF (globalDebug AND debugInit) <> 0 THEN
         DO;
          CALL ConLineOut(
                @('Dlc New link Configured: '),
                24);
          CALL ConHexOut(DOUBLE(linkNumber));
          CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
         END;
$ENDIF
       END;
      ELSE
       DO;
        /* set up error word */
        error = ConfigureDlCB.reqError;
       END;

      IF error = 0 THEN
       DO;
        error2 = 0;
        x = 0;
        DO WHILE (x < ConfigureDlCB.numberOfBuffers) AND
                      (error2 = 0);
         pRecvDlCB = OsAllocate(
           (ConfigureDlCB.bufferSize + SIZE(recvDlCB)),
           @error2);
         IF error2 = 0 THEN 
          DO;
           recvDlCB.linkNumber =
                  configureDlCB.linkNumber;
           recvDlCB.stationNumber = noStationAddress;
           recvDlCB.dataLength = msgNoBufferPtr OR 0;
           recvDlCB.bufferLength = 
                  configureDlCB.bufferSize;
           recvDlCB.ipcCode = msgNetworkIo;
           recvDlCB.freeDisp = returnMsg;
           x = x + 1;
           CALL GenGiveToDlc(linkNumber, 
              (dlcReceive OR msgRequest),
              SELECTOR$OF(pRecvDlCB), @error2);
          END;
         ELSE 
          DO;
           CALL OsLogError(3, osOutOfMem, SHL(DOUBLE(linkNumber), 8) OR 0FFh, @(6, 'dlcbuf'));
$IF debugging
           IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN
            DO;
             CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc out of buffer space', 0Ah, 0Dh), 25);
            END;
$ENDIF
          END;
        END;
       END;
     END;
    ConfigureDlCB.sourcePID = tempPID;
    ConfigureDlCB.msgFormat = tempMsgFormat;
    ConfigureDlCB.freeDisp = tempFreeDisp;
   END;

  /* if configured ok and not specified to not report init to commexec,
      then send initialized message to commexec */
  IF error = ok THEN
   DO;
    IF configOption <> noteConfigOnly THEN
     DO;
	  commExecName(commExecName(0)) = numberArray(OsCardNumber);
      commexecPid = OsLookUpName(@commExecName, @error2);
      IF error2 = ok THEN
       DO;
        pInitDlCB = UtlBuildCB;
        initDlCB.ipcCode = msgNetworkIo;
        initDlCB.freeDisp = freeMsg;
        initDlCB.linkNumber = linkNumber;
        initDlCB.stationNumber = noStationAddress;
        initDlCB.protocolPid = dlcProcessId(linkNumber);
        initDlCB.pDlCBfreeQueue = pCbFreeQueue;
        initDlCB.protocolType = ConfigureDlCB.protocolType;
        CALL OsSend(commExecPid, 
             (dlcInitialize OR msgResponse), 0,
             BUILD$PTR(pInitDlCB, 0), @error2);
        IF error2 <> ok THEN pInitDlCB = UtlFreeCB(pInitDlCB);
       END;
$IF debugging
      IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN
       DO;
        CALL ConLineOut(@('Dlc Init Reported: '), 19);
        CALL ConHexOut(error);
        CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
       END;
$ENDIF
     END;
   END;
  ELSE
   DO;
$IF debugging
    IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN
     DO;
      CALL ConLineOut(@('New link Configure Failed: '), 27);
      CALL ConHexOut(error);
      CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
     END;
$ENDIF
    CALL OsLogError(2, error, SHL(DOUBLE(linkNumber), 8) OR 0FFh, @(6,'dlcCon'));
    CALL MacDisable(linkNumber);
    CALL OsDeleteProcess(dlcProcessId(linkNumber), @error2);
    dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = null;
   END;
 END;
END HandleDlcConfigure;

/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

HandleDlcInit: PROCEDURE (pInitDlCB, pError);
 DCL pInitDlCB SELECTOR;
 DCL initDlCB BASED pInitDlCB STRUCTURE (DlCBgenDescriptor,
                DlCBinitParams);
 DCL pError POINTER;
 DCL error BASED pError WORD;
 DCL linkNumber BYTE;
 DO;
  error = ok;
  linkNumber = initDlCB.linkNumber;
  IF (linkNumber >= maxNumberOfLinks) THEN 
    error = eDlcInvalidLinkNumber;
  ELSE IF dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = null THEN
    error = eDlcNotInitialized;
  ELSE 
   DO;
    initDlCB.protocolPid = dlcProcessId(linkNumber);
    initDlCB.pDlCBfreeQueue = pCbFreeQueue;
   END;
  IF error <> 0 THEN
    CALL OsLogError(2, error, SHL(DOUBLE(linkNumber), 8) OR 0FFh, @(6,'dlcIni'));
 END;

END HandleDlcInit;

/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

HandleDlcShut: PROCEDURE (pShutDlCB, pError);
 DCL pShutDlCB SELECTOR;
 DCL pError POINTER;
 DCL linkNumber BYTE; 
 DCL error BASED pError WORD;

$IF document
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Purpose: This procedure allows the caller to shut the data link
      process completely down. 

 Inputs:  Selector of the shut control block msg. This message will
      include the following parameters:
       linkNumber - port to which shut down shoulf be issed).
       clean up - boolean flag specifying whether protocol 
          should gracefully shut down or not.

 Algorithm: o Send a message to the data link process notifying it of
      the impending shutdown.
      o wait for response.
      o delete process and any resources associated with it.
      o return message to original caller.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
$ENDIF
 DCL shutDlCB BASED pShutDlCB STRUCTURE (DlCBGenDescriptor);
 DCL (tempPID, note, tempMsgFormat) WORD;
 DCL tempFreeDisp BYTE;
 DCL x BYTE;

 DO;
  linkNumber = shutDlCB.linkNumber;
  IF (linkNumber >= maxNumberOfLinks) THEN 
    error = eDlcInvalidLinkNumber;
  ELSE IF dlcProcessId(dlCB.linkNumber) <> null THEN
   DO;
    tempPID = shutDlCB.sourcePID;
    tempmsgFormat = shutDlCB.msgFormat;
    tempFreeDisp = shutDlCB.freeDisp;
    shutDlCB.freeDisp = returnMsg;
    CALL GenGiveToDlc(linkNumber, (dlcDie OR msgRequest),
          pShutDlCB, @error);
    pShutDlCB = SELECTOR$OF(OsReceive(dlcProcessId(linkNumber),
            anyClass, 10000, @note, @error));
$IF phoneLink
    IF dlcProcessId(linkNumber) <> phoneLinkProcess THEN
$ENDIF
     CALL OsDeleteProcess(dlcProcessId(linkNumber), @error);
    dlcProcessId(linkNumber) = null;
    CALL MacDisable(linkNumber);
    shutDlCB.sourcePID = tempPID;
    shutDlCB.msgFormat = tempMsgFormat;
    shutDlCB.freeDisp = tempFreeDisp;
  IF error <> 0 THEN
    CALL OsLogError(2, error, SHL(DOUBLE(linkNumber), 8) OR 0FFh, @(6,'dlcSht'));
   END;
 END;
END HandleDlcShut;

/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

HandleNmRequest: PROCEDURE (pNmDlCB, pError);
 DCL pNmDlCB SELECTOR;
 DCL pError POINTER;
 DCL error BASED pError WORD;
 DCL dlCB BASED pNmDlCB STRUCTURE (dlCBGenDescriptor,
               buffer (1) BYTE);
 DCL (linkNumber, stationNumber) BYTE;
 DCL (msgType, layer, nmLength) WORD;
 DCL pNmData POINTER;
 DCL nmData BASED pNmData (1) BYTE;
 DCL pDlcStats POINTER;
 DCL dlcStats BASED pDlcStats (1) STRUCTURE (DlCBStatsParams);
 DCL pDlcMachineArray POINTER;
 DCL dlcMachineArray BASED pDlcMachineArray (1) SELECTOR;
 DCL pDlcMachine SELECTOR;
 DCL dlcMachine BASED pDlcMachine generalMachineType;
 DCL x WORD;
 DO;
  IF (dlCB.msgFormat AND msgFormatReqRspMask) = msgResponse THEN
   DO;
    error = eDlcInvalidRequest;
    RETURN;
   END;
  layer = dlCB.msgFormat AND msgNmLayerMask;
  msgType = dlCB.msgFormat AND msgNmFormatMask;

  IF (msgType = msgNmReadCtrs) OR (msgType = msgNmReadResetCtrs) THEN
   DO;
    IF (layer = nmMacLayer) THEN
     DO;
      IF dlCB.linkNumber = anyLinkNumber THEN
       DO;
        nmLength = SIZE(macStatistics);
        pNmData = @macStatistics;
       END;
      ELSE
       DO;
        nmLength = SIZE(macStatistics(0));
        pNmData = @macStatistics(dlCB.linkNumber);
       END;
      IF nmLength > dlCB.bufferLength THEN 
         nmLength = (dlCB.bufferLength MOD
         SIZE(macStatistics(0))) *  SIZE(macStatistics(0));
      CALL MOVB(pNmData, @dlCB.buffer, nmLength);
      dlCB.bufferLength = nmLength;
     END;
    ELSE IF (layer = nmDlcLayer) THEN
     DO;
      pDlcMachineArray = globalStateMachinePtr(dlCB.linkNumber);
      pDlcStats = @dlCB.buffer;
      IF dlCB.linkNumber = anyLinkNumber THEN
       DO;
        error = eDlcInvalidRequest;
       END;
      ELSE IF (pDlcMachineArray = NIL) OR
        (dlCB.linkNumber > (maxNumberOfLinks - 1)) THEN
       DO;
        error = eDlcNotInitialized;
       END;
      ELSE
       /* do max number of stations, minus station for
        handling too many stations condition */
       DO x = 0 TO (maxNumberOfStations - 2);
        IF (pDlcMachine := dlcMachineArray(x)) <> null THEN
         DO;
          dlcStats(x).state = dlcMachine.state;
          dlcStats(x).linkAddress = dlcMachine.linkAddress;
          dlcStats(x).connected = dlcMachine.connected;
          CALL MOVW(@dlcMachine.sendCounter, @dlcStats(x).counters, 16);
         END;
        ELSE
         DO;
          dlcStats(x).state = 0;
          dlcStats(x).linkAddress = 0;
          dlcStats(x).connected = FALSE;
          CALL SETW(0, @dlcStats(x).counters, 16);
         END;
       END;
     END;
   END;

  IF (msgType = msgNmResetCtrs) OR (msgType = msgNmReadResetCtrs) THEN
   DO;
    IF (layer = nmMacLayer) THEN
     DO;
      IF dlCB.linkNumber = anyLinkNumber THEN
       DO;
        nmLength = SIZE(macStatistics);
        pNmData = @macStatistics;
       END;
      ELSE
       DO;
        nmLength = SIZE(macStatistics(0));
        pNmData = @macStatistics(dlCB.linkNumber);
       END;
      DISABLE;
       CALL SETB(0, pNmData, nmLength);
      ENABLE;
     END;
    ELSE IF (layer = nmDlcLayer) THEN
     DO;
      pDlcMachineArray = globalStateMachinePtr(dlCB.linkNumber);
      IF dlCB.linkNumber = anyLinkNumber THEN
       DO;
        error = eDlcInvalidRequest;
       END;
      ELSE IF pDlcMachineArray <> NIL THEN
       DO x = 0 TO (maxNumberOfStations - 2);
        IF (pDlcMachine := dlcMachineArray(x)) <> null THEN
         DO;
          DISABLE;
           CALL SETW(0, @dlcMachine.sendCounter, 16);
          ENABLE;
         END;
       END;
     END;
   END;
 END;
END HandleNmRequest;

/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

DlcProcess: PROCEDURE CLEAN;
 DO;
$IF document
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Initialization Algorithm
 ------------------------

 1) add name of master dlc to name table ('dlc').
 2) create timer process for dlc timer management.
 3) allocate data link message control block pool
 4) do global initialization of the data link hardware and
  control structures.
 5) While shutdown message not received do:
  1) wait for new message
  2) if initialization request then process init.
  3) if shutdown message then exit loop.
  4) if status message the process status.
 6) perform dlc shut down and clean up.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
$ENDIF

 /* print version string */
$IF debugging2
  DO;
   DCL pSeg POINTER;
   DCL pSegDW DWORD AT (@pSeg);
   CALL ConLineOut(@('Dlc Version '), 12);
   CALL ConLineOut(@dlcVersionStr(1), dlcVersionStr(0));
   CALL ConLineOut(@(0Ah, 0Dh), 2);
   CALL ConLineOut(@('Mac Version '), 12);
   CALL ConLineOut(@MacVersionStr(1), macVersionStr(0));
   CALL ConLineOut(@(0Ah, 0Dh), 2);

   pSeg = @DlcProcess;
   CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc segment is: '), 16);
   CALL ConHexOut(HIGH(pSegDW));
   CALL ConCharOut(':');
   CALL ConHexOut(LOW(pSegDW));   
   CALL ConLineOut(@(', debug mask: '), 14);
   CALL ConHexOut(globalDebug);
   CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
  END;
$ENDIF
$IF debugging
  CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc Pid: '), 9);
  CALL ConHexOut(OsWhoAmI);
  CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
$ENDIF

  CALL OsHandleCancel(FALSE);
  dlcMgrName(dlcMgrName(0)) = numberArray(OsCardNumber);

$IF debugging
  CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc registering: '), 17);
  CALL ConLineOut(@dlcMgrName(1), dlcMgrName(0));
  CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
$ENDIF
  CALL OsRegisterName(@dlcMgrName, NIL, 2, @error);
  CALL OsRegisterName(@dlcMgrName, DOUBLE(OsWhoAmI), 1, @error);


  macMgrName(macMgrName(0)) = numberArray(OsCardNumber);

$IF debugging
  CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc registering: '), 17);
  CALL ConLineOut(@MacMgrName(1), MacMgrName(0));
  CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
$ENDIF
  CALL OsRegisterName(@MacMgrName, NIL, 2, @error);
  CALL OsRegisterName(@macMgrName, DOUBLE(OsWhoAmI), 1, @error);


  CALL MacGlobalEnable(@error);
  IF error <> ok THEN 
   DO;
$IF debugging
    IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN 
     DO;
      CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc cant initialize Mac: '), 26);
      CALL ConHexOut(error);
      CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
     END;
$ENDIF
    GOTO errorExit;
   END;
$IF debugging
  CALL ConLineOut(@('Mac Enabled', 0Ah, 0Dh), 13);
$ENDIF

  pCbFreeQueue = MemAllocateMemory(80, 48, @error);
  IF error <> ok THEN
   DO;
$IF debugging
    IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN 
     DO;
      CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc cant initialize cbQ: '), 26);
      CALL ConHexOut(error);
      CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
     END;
$ENDIF
    GOTO errorExit;
   END;
$IF debugging2
  DO;
   DCL wMemArea WORD AT (@pCbFreeQueue);
   CALL ConLineOut(@('Control Block Area at: '), 23);
   CALL ConHexOut(wMemArea);
   CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
  END;
$ENDIF
  
  CALL TmrEnableTimer(@error);
  IF error <> ok THEN 
   DO;
$IF debugging
    IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN 
     DO;
      CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc cant initialize Tmr: '), 26);
      CALL ConHexOut(error);
      CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
     END;
$ENDIF
    GOTO errorExit;
   END;
$IF debugging
  CALL ConLineOut(@('Timer Enabled', 0Ah, 0Dh), 15);
$ENDIF

  /* ensure dlc dad processing of important requests */
  CALL OsSetPriority(OsWhoAmI, 20, @error);
  
  shutDown = FALSE;
  DO WHILE NOT shutdown;
   pDlCB = SELECTOR$OF(OsReceive(anyProcess, anyClass,
           waitforever, @note, @error));
   IF error = ok THEN
    DO;
     logError = FALSE;
     IF (dlCB.msgFormat = dlcInitialize) THEN
       CALL HandleDlcInit(pDlCB, @error);
     ELSE IF (dlCB.msgFormat = dlcShutdown) THEN
       CALL HandleDlcShut(pDlCB, @error);
     ELSE IF dlCB.msgFormat = dlcDie THEN
       shutDown = TRUE;
     ELSE IF dlCB.msgFormat = (msgNmConfig OR msgRequest) THEN
       CALL HandleDlcConfigure(pDlCB, @error);
     ELSE IF dlCB.msgFormat = (msgNmDebug OR msgRequest) THEN
      DO;
       /* print version string */
       CALL ConLineOut(@('Dlc Version '), 12);
       CALL ConLineOut(@dlcVersionStr(1), dlcVersionStr(0));
       CALL ConLineOut(@(0Ah, 0Dh), 2);
       CALL ConLineOut(@('Mac Version '), 12);
       CALL ConLineOut(@MacVersionStr(1), macVersionStr(0));
       CALL ConLineOut(@(0Ah, 0Dh), 2);
       error = globalDebug;
       globalDebug = note;
      END;
        /* handle all other network mgmt request types */
     ELSE IF (dlCB.msgFormat AND msgClassMask) = classNM THEN
       CALL HandleNmRequest(pDlCB, @error);
     ELSE /* nothing else supported right now */
      DO;
       error = eDlcInvalidRequest;
       logError = TRUE;
$IF debugging
       IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN
        DO;
         DCL wDlCB WORD AT(@pDlCB);
         CALL ConLineOut(
              @('dlcdad Invalid Class: '), 22);
         CALL ConHexOut(dlCB.msgFormat);
         CALL ConLineOut(@(', ptr = '), 8);
         CALL ConHexOut(wDlCB);
         CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
        END;
$ENDIF
      END;
     IF (error <> 0) AND logError THEN
      CALL OsLogError(2, error, note, @(6,'dlcMsg'));

     IF dlCB.sourcePid <> OsWhoAmI THEN
      CALL OsSend(dlCB.sourcePid,
           (dlCB.msgFormat OR msgResponse),
           error, BUILD$PTR(pDlCB, 0), @error);
     ELSE CALL OsFree(BUILD$PTR(pDlCB, 0), @error);
    END;
  END;

normalExit:
  CALL MacGlobalDisable;
  RETURN;

errorExit:
  CALL OsLogError(2, error, 0, @(6,'dlcDad'));
$IF debugging
  IF (globalDebug AND debugErrors) <> 0 THEN 
   DO;
    CALL ConLineOut(@('dlc Error Condition: '), 21);
    CALL ConHexOut(error);
    CALL ConLineOut(@(0Dh, 0Ah), 2);
   END;
$ENDIF
  GOTO normalExit;

 END;
END DlcProcess;

/*@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@*/

$IF CompassCentral
 CALL DlcProcess;
 CALL OsExit(0);
$ENDIF

END DlcModule;
